@startuml
title v0001-executor-docker - Docker Executor topology (MVP, health-probe REST API)

participant "Mocked task server\n(Router / State Registry / Env Registry)" as Mock
participant "Docker Executor\n(Go process)\nlocalhost:8020 = livez/readyz" as Ex
participant "Docker daemon" as Docker
participant "OpenHands containers\n(up to EXECUTOR_MAX_CONTAINERS)\nREST/WS on :8000 each" as OH

Ex -> Docker : pull image
Ex -> Docker : docker run per accepted task\nlabels: executor_id, runtime, task_id\npublish :8000 -> distinct host port
Docker -> OH : start OpenHands runtimes
Ex -> OH : GET /health per container (wait until ready)
Ex -> Mock : PUT /v1/executors/{executor_id} (State Registry record)
Ex -> Mock : POST /v1/executors/{executor_id}/events (executor.healthy)
Ex -> Mock : GET /v1/tasks?filter=openhands (list Router workload)
Mock --> Ex : matching tasks with pending_actions
Ex -> OH : POST each accepted task via that container's OpenHands REST API
OH --> Ex : per-task events (LLM calls, tool use, status)
Ex -> Mock : POST /v1/tasks/{task_id}/events (forward OpenHands events)
OH --> Ex : terminal status
Ex -> Mock : POST /v1/tasks/{task_id}/events (task.finished / task.failed)

note over Mock, Ex
  Router tasks, not Executor REST endpoints, drive controls:
  - queued task -> Ex starts per-task OpenHands container if capacity free
  - pending interrupt_task -> Ex POSTs OPENHANDS_INTERRUPT_ENDPOINT
  - pending append_task_message -> Ex POSTs OPENHANDS_MESSAGE_ENDPOINT
end note

note over Ex
  Single Executor process = bounded worker pool.
  Max concurrent containers = EXECUTOR_MAX_CONTAINERS.
  SIGTERM drains all owned containers before shutdown.
end note

note over Mock
  Three surfaces in v0001:
  - Router (eventually v0004)
  - State Registry (eventually v0002)
  - Env Registry (eventually v0003)
end note

@enduml
